WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.860
Thanks for tuning in to Tesla Short's Time, episode 542 for July 15th, 2026.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.580
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Here's what you need to know about Tesla today.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.680
Tesla posted its best second quarter ever as the energy business spiked sharply higher.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.520
Tesla reported its strongest second quarter on record, driven in part by a sharp rise in energy

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.260
deployments. The company also set the date for its upcoming earnings call.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.420
This result shows the non-vehicle side of the business continuing to scale while vehicle

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:40.360
margins stabilize. Listeners tracking the energy program will want to hear how mega-packed

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:46.040
production and power-wall attachments factor into the quarter. The earnings call will provide

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.600
the next concrete data point on whether this momentum holds. With the energy segment now

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.500
delivering real scale, let's look at how the vehicle side is holding up on pricing.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.360
Kelly Blue Book Data shows Tesla's average transaction price rose slightly in June

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:11.720
to $53,107. The year-over-year drop of 2.1% is the smallest of the year while the broader EV

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:22.940
market fell 4.5%. Model Y averaged $51,775 and still accounted for over 35% of all EV sales.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.800
The report indicates Tesla has moved past the deepest discount phase while protecting margins

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.500
better than rivals. While pricing stabilizes, software development keeps moving quickly.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:42.280
Software Update 2026.20.6.6 is rolling out with the latest FSD supervised branch.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.940
Early drivers are testing the new version on both HW3 and HW4 vehicles.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:54.840
The release continues the rapid iteration cycle that has defined the supervised program since

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:01.620
the V12 series. Next data point to watch is how widely the update spreads before the next branch

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:09.760
appears. Tesla is running distilled versions of its FSD models on HW4 hardware as part of the push

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:16.040
toward unsupervised capability across fleets. The approach reveals how the company is managing

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:21.880
inference across different vehicle generations. It directly addresses one of the open questions

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:28.060
around whether current hardware can support the next regulatory step. Watch for any public comments

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:35.140
on how distillation affects latency or edge case handling. On the hardware side, one fleet operator

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:41.360
is already putting Tesla's newest vehicle to work. Paper transport has added Tesla semis to

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.500
its fleet under a new pilot program. The deployment is aimed at cutting emissions on specific routes

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:53.940
while real-world range and total cost of ownership data are collected. This adds to the small but

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:59.940
growing set of commercial operators testing the truck. The next milestone will be whether additional

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:07.060
fleets sign on after seeing these early results. The Model Y continues to show similar real-world

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:13.660
strength in passenger markets. The Model Y remains the top seller in Europe's growing midsize SUV

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:19.360
category. Chinese brands have doubled their share in the same segment over the past year.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:25.760
The result shows Tesla holding volume leadership even as new competitors enter. It also

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.460
highlights how regional demand patterns are shifting for the vehicle platform. South Korea's

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:38.400
eco-friendly vehicle exports passed 100,000 units this period. The Model Y placed second

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:44.680
in domestic EV sales despite limited local production. The ranking reflects sustained demand

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:51.400
even as global supply chains adjust. It also shows how Tesla's core vehicle platform continues

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:57.900
to perform across multiple markets. A separate report noted that a lower-priced Model Y variant

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:03.160
brings the price down along with the content. Reviewers examine the entry-level version

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:09.060
and noted reduced content compared with higher trims. The changes include simpler materials

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:15.500
and fewer standard features. The test shows how Tesla is executing its cost-reduction strategy

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:21.460
on an existing platform. Buyers will weigh whether the lower price justifies the trimmed

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:29.300
specification. That competitive pressure now extends beyond cars. Buid outlined its strategy to

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:35.820
challenge Tesla in humanoid robotics with its own manufacturing scale. The company is leveraging

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:41.920
existing EV production lines to accelerate robot development. This marks a direct competitive

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:48.860
response to Tesla's optimist timeline. Observers will watch whether Buid's approach narrows the gap

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:55.620
in real-world deployment speed. Meanwhile, regulatory and incentive rules are creating uneven conditions

00:04:55.620 --> 00:05:02.340
for Tesla owners. California's updated rebate program excludes Tesla vehicles while including

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:08.840
Rivian and Lucid models. The change stems from rules around manufacturer location and sales

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:15.880
thresholds. Tesla owners in the state will not receive the $3,500 incentive available to some

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:22.260
competitors. The policy shift shows how regulatory design can create uneven competitive conditions

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:29.300
even for market leaders. Smaller operational hiccups also continue to surface. A pricing glitch

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:35.560
caused some Canadian supercharger sessions to build higher than expected. Tesla has begun refunding

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:40.700
affected drivers. The incident highlights ongoing operational challenges in maintaining

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:46.660
consistent pricing across the network. Reliability of the billing system will remain a watch item

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:53.900
as open access usage grows. One owner shared a clip of FSD quickly swirving around a construction

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:59.320
barricade that landed on the highway. The maneuver happened in seconds without driver input.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:06.300
The incident adds to the growing list of real-world edge cases the system is handling. It also underscores

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:12.400
why owners keep sharing these clips as evidence of incremental progress. Discussions on Reddit noted

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:20.120
that FSD-V14 light remains in limited release even when it shows good performance on HW3 cars.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:28.040
Owners report that the limited release of FSD-V14 light continues despite strong HW3 results.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.220
The decision keeps the branch from wider distribution for now. It raises questions about what

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:40.460
additional validation Tesla wants before expanding access. The thread shows community patience

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:47.300
is wearing thin on the pace of broader rollout. A rare early model S signature addition appeared on

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:54.440
the resale market with an asking price above $260,000. The listing highlights how certain low

00:06:54.440 --> 00:07:00.780
mileage early production vehicles retain collector interest. It also shows the wide range of values

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:05.960
that exist within the used Tesla market. The outcome will test whether buyers are willing

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:11.560
to pay a premium for historical significance. An experienced technician compared charging

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:18.860
stops on a long Ioniq 6 trip and found Tesla sites added minor delays. The comment came despite

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:24.520
the network's widespread availability. It points to differences in charging speed and sight layout

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:30.900
that some drivers still notice. The observation offers a rare non-Tesla perspective on how the

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:37.380
network performs under real travel conditions. Lucid denied reports that it was considering bankruptcy

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:43.460
after its stock fell more than 40%. The company's communications director issued a direct

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:49.680
rebuttal to the earlier story. It also serves as a reminder of the capital intensity still facing

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:56.900
the broader sector. Chamath Polyhapidea publicly stated that a Tesla SpaceX merger makes obvious

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:04.000
strategic sense. The comment came as TSLA shares Rose overnight following several analysts target

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:10.600
increases. The idea revives a long discussed structural possibility without any confirmation from

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:16.120
either company. Investors will look for any further signals in upcoming earnings commentary.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:22.200
Before we wrap, here's a quick counterpoint on valuation. The Motley Fool argues that

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:27.760
another luxury automaker offers better near-term prospects than Tesla for investors focused

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:33.460
on traditional vehicle metrics. It highlights differences in brand positioning and current product

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:39.100
cycles. The piece reflects ongoing debate about whether Tesla's valuation should be judged

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:45.220
primarily on its auto business or on future programs. Tesla will need to deliver visible

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:51.060
progress on those programs to shift this narrative. Energy storage economics have long been

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:57.160
framed as a question of raw sell cost per kilowatt hour. Tesla's latest quarter shows the

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:02.520
energy segment contributing meaningfully to overall results, even while vehicle pricing pressure

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:08.960
continues. The distinction matters because storage margins depend less on per unit vehicle complexity

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:14.360
and more on repeatable project execution and software services layered on top of hardware.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:20.040
When storage revenue grows faster than the auto business, it changes the capital allocation

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:25.140
picture for the company as a whole. The conventional view treats energy as a side

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:31.200
business that rides along with vehicle scale. In practice, Megapack and Powerwall deployments

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:36.460
create their own demand signals through utility contracts and residential virtual power plants.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:42.680
These channels do not require the same distribution network or brand marketing spend that vehicles

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:49.000
demand. The result is a margin profile that can remain resilient even when average transaction

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:55.000
prices on cars are flat or declining. Investors watching only vehicle delivery numbers

00:09:55.000 --> 00:10:00.400
therefore miss the second engine that is already running. If energy keeps compounding at its

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.680
current rate, the business mix inside Tesla shifts without any single headline event.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:11.580
That shift is what ultimately determines how much of future cash flow comes from hardware sales

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:17.940
versus recurring services. Tomorrow, keep an eye on the earnings call for fresh details on energy

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:23.720
deployments and whether vehicle margins continue to stabilize. That's your Tesla news for today.

